This work introduces a Monte Carlo-based approach for predicting residual dipolar couplings in weakly aligned molecules. By explicitly accounting for molecular flexibility and intermolecular interactions governing alignment, the method provides an efficient route to connect molecular structure and dynamics with experimentally accessible RDCs.
